@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/model-serving>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "model-serving"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The model-serving slice of the GMEOW ontology (extension tier): a thin, standalone LLM-operations vocabulary reusable by anyone modelling model serving, with nothing to do with inhabitation. It gives the served model artifact, its deployment (a relator), a runtime execution (an occurrent), and an agent session (an event aggregate) each an explicit identity — rather than collapsing them onto a single gmeow:AwarenessTenure — and splits the gmeow:ModelCard relations so a distribution is not inferred a software agent. gmeow:ModelInvocation (core ai) is reused at the instance level (Principle 5). Depends only on core, so it is a DAG-legal extension → core: gmeow:sliceDependsOn names core slices only, and no artifact that carries a semantic dependency edge — module, shapes, mappings, competency or verify queries — names a sibling extension's term. The CQ5 capability-versus-delegation question, whose delegation half is the agentic slice's gmeow:ToolCall / gmeow:usedTool, is therefore answered one level out in slices/profile/agent-runtime, the profile that selects both extensions and mints nothing. Authored from the ratified design set (INHABITED-RUNTIME-STACK.md)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/model-serving> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Model-Serving Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierExtension ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/entities> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/ai> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/events> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/provenance> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "The LLM-ops / AI-agent audience (Principle 15): anyone modelling model serving — the served artifact, its deployment, the runtime execution, and the agent session — who needs to trace an output to the exact artifact·deployment·execution·session·invocation that produced it. The gmeow agent-runtime profile is its first live consumer, composing it with core/inhabitation so an output resolves to the durable subject; the OpenTelemetry-GenAI observability seam is its interchange consumer."@x-gmeow-english .
